                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://homotopy.io"}> homotopy.io
                , original tool
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://beta.homotopy.io"}> beta.homotopy.io
                , updated tool
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/homotopy-io"}> github.com/homotopy-io
                , codebase
          %p
            It is based on the theory of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+n-categories"}
                associative
                = succeed "-categories" do
                  %em n
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopies"} homotopies
            of composites, which have a direct geometrical interpretation. The proof assistant allows the user to define
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} generators
            for a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category"} higher category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} compose
            them, apply
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopies"} homotopies
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagrams"} string diagrams
            in 2 dimensions or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface+diagrams"} surface diagrams
            in 3 dimensions. Interaction with the proof assistant is entirely by direct manipulation using the mouse.
          %p
            It can be considered a successor to the existing proof assistant
            = succeed "," do
